<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization (Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre))" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-6> ;
    schema:about "Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D phase-field of the chitin membrane, resolution of individual mineral bridges, a derived (not templated) gastropod tower lattice, a time-dependent eikonal or BCF step-flow simulation, literature-digitised species pitch/omega observations, an independently calibrated SEM scale, or validated values of e_6, S_0, beta or the pore statistics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form Cabrera-Levine phase fields for single screw, supercritical/subcritical Frank-Read dipoles and same-chirality pairs on a 2D grid with contour winding integrals, an optional direction-dependent step speed A(theta) with single-domain or {110} cyclic-twin averaging, a closed-terrace-ring Fourier polygonization measurement, a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn perforation model whose per-sheet footprint is slaved to the terrace tier and whose bridge site is the early-phi argmax, a sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep, a 12-species BCF pitch/omega regression, a DoG lamellar-seam segmentation of one SEM micrograph, and 7 Lean 4 theorems on the integer/rational skeleton of these laws",
        "reported_in_source: Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): Gibbs-Thomson curved-step velocity v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the rotating Archimedean spiral with pitch lambda_0 = (2 pi / omega_0) r_c ~ 19 r_c",
        "reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre grows by Burton-Cabrera-Frank screw-dislocation spiral and target terraces on the mineral surface, with a periodic stack of beta-chitin inter-lamellar membranes (h_0 ~ 0.5 um) whose pores admit mineral bridges that nucleate the next tablet (Sec. 4); columnar (gastropod) nacre stacks tablets vertically, sheet (bivalve) nacre staggers them like bricks",
        "reported_in_source: Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw dislocations and Frank-Read-type dislocation pairs; opposite-chirality pairs separated by more than 2 r_c emit closed target terraces",
        "reported_in_source: Checa, Cartwright & Willinger (2011) and Schäffer et al. (1997): mineral bridges (tens of nm) pass through pores of the inter-lamellar membrane and connect vertically stacked tablets",
        "reported_in_source: De Villiers (1971): orthorhombic aragonite lattice constants a = 4.9611, b = 7.9672, c = 5.7407 A",
        "transfer_boundary: The 'eikonal solver' is kinematic: terrace phases are closed-form Cabrera-Levine travel functions divided by A(theta), not a time-stepped front-propagation PDE, and the subcritical vs supercritical dipole regime is selected by an `if` on d <= 2 r_c rather than emerging from the dynamics",
        "transfer_boundary: The 12-species lambda_obs / omega_obs table is within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and is not traceable to a measured table in the cited papers; r = 0.9999 therefore tests the table's construction, not the biology",
        "transfer_boundary: The SEM um/px calibration (0.019867 um/px) was anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um because the Wikimedia micrograph has no scale bar; only the dimensionless CV and aspect ratio are calibration-independent",
        "transfer_boundary: The membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets (no through-thickness phi(z)) at dx = 0.1875 um, so a perforation patch stands for a cluster of 40-60 nm bridges; the bridge site is the argmax of early phi, not a resolved growth-through-pore process; S_0, beta, eps, pore amplitude/width/density are model parameters tuned so that both regimes perforate on the grid",
        "transfer_boundary: e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic anisotropy amplitude; twin averaging is a mean-field superposition of A(theta) with no explicit twin boundaries in the spiral core" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jsb.2011.09.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1021/cm960429i>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0900867106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2006.0188>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsta.1951.0006>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsta.2011.0600> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-13>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-14>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-15>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Burton-Cabrera-Frank (BCF) Screw-Dislocation Eikonal Step-Flow & Chiral Defect Pair Dynamics" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 8.52e-01 .

