<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization (Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre))",
        "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization faithfully reproduces Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 85.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py> ;
    schema:about "Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D phase-field of the chitin membrane, resolution of individual mineral bridges, a derived (not templated) gastropod tower lattice, a time-dependent eikonal or BCF step-flow simulation, literature-digitised species pitch/omega observations, an independently calibrated SEM scale, or validated values of e_6, S_0, beta or the pore statistics",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form Cabrera-Levine phase fields for single screw, supercritical/subcritical Frank-Read dipoles and same-chirality pairs on a 2D grid with contour winding integrals, an optional direction-dependent step speed A(theta) with single-domain or {110} cyclic-twin averaging, a closed-terrace-ring Fourier polygonization measurement, a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn perforation model whose per-sheet footprint is slaved to the terrace tier and whose bridge site is the early-phi argmax, a sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep, a 12-species BCF pitch/omega regression, a DoG lamellar-seam segmentation of one SEM micrograph, and 7 Lean 4 theorems on the integer/rational skeleton of these laws",
        "reported_in_source: Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): Gibbs-Thomson curved-step velocity v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the rotating Archimedean spiral with pitch lambda_0 = (2 pi / omega_0) r_c ~ 19 r_c",
        "reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre grows by Burton-Cabrera-Frank screw-dislocation spiral and target terraces on the mineral surface, with a periodic stack of beta-chitin inter-lamellar membranes (h_0 ~ 0.5 um) whose pores admit mineral bridges that nucleate the next tablet (Sec. 4); columnar (gastropod) nacre stacks tablets vertically, sheet (bivalve) nacre staggers them like bricks",
        "reported_in_source: Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw dislocations and Frank-Read-type dislocation pairs; opposite-chirality pairs separated by more than 2 r_c emit closed target terraces",
        "reported_in_source: Checa, Cartwright & Willinger (2011) and Schäffer et al. (1997): mineral bridges (tens of nm) pass through pores of the inter-lamellar membrane and connect vertically stacked tablets",
        "reported_in_source: De Villiers (1971): orthorhombic aragonite lattice constants a = 4.9611, b = 7.9672, c = 5.7407 A",
        "transfer_boundary: The 'eikonal solver' is kinematic: terrace phases are closed-form Cabrera-Levine travel functions divided by A(theta), not a time-stepped front-propagation PDE, and the subcritical vs supercritical dipole regime is selected by an `if` on d <= 2 r_c rather than emerging from the dynamics",
        "transfer_boundary: The 12-species lambda_obs / omega_obs table is within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and is not traceable to a measured table in the cited papers; r = 0.9999 therefore tests the table's construction, not the biology",
        "transfer_boundary: The SEM um/px calibration (0.019867 um/px) was anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um because the Wikimedia micrograph has no scale bar; only the dimensionless CV and aspect ratio are calibration-independent",
        "transfer_boundary: The membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets (no through-thickness phi(z)) at dx = 0.1875 um, so a perforation patch stands for a cluster of 40-60 nm bridges; the bridge site is the argmax of early phi, not a resolved growth-through-pore process; S_0, beta, eps, pore amplitude/width/density are model parameters tuned so that both regimes perforate on the grid",
        "transfer_boundary: e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic anisotropy amplitude; twin averaging is a mean-field superposition of A(theta) with no explicit twin boundaries in the spiral core" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py; output: docs/media/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_comparison.png; organism: Pteria hirundo & Pinctada margaritifera (Bivalvia sheet nacre) / Haliotis rufescens & Gibbula umbilicalis (Gastropoda tower nacre); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 4c231c8398be9a26483bc4175fe15077a90c9e9b18a12deaf2c2e4265b43d447; artifact_sha256: 783e8dff611789f803e2347b93f2a800d17da83e277f9b6edc9ca0174d15f68b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_aragonite_tablets_specimen.jpg=e4c6590464523f21..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json=580b05d6121d9596..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/scout_manifest.json=6084a2ce133990fc...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre grows by Burton-Cabrera-Frank screw-dislocation spiral and target terraces on the mineral surface, with a periodic stack of beta-chitin inter-lamellar membranes (h_0 ~ 0.5 um) whose pores admit mineral bridges that nucleate the next tablet (Sec. 4); columnar (gastropod) nacre stacks tablets vertically, sheet (bivalve) nacre staggers them like bricks | Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw dislocations and Frank-Read-type dislocation pairs; opposite-chirality pairs separated by more than 2 r_c emit closed target terraces | Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): Gibbs-Thomson curved-step velocity v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the rotating Archimedean spiral with pitch lambda_0 = (2 pi / omega_0) r_c ~ 19 r_c | Checa, Cartwright & Willinger (2011) and Schäffer et al. (1997): mineral bridges (tens of nm) pass through pores of the inter-lamellar membrane and connect vertically stacked tablets | De Villiers (1971): orthorhombic aragonite lattice constants a = 4.9611, b = 7.9672, c = 5.7407 A; reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form Cabrera-Levine phase fields for single screw, supercritical/subcritical Frank-Read dipoles and same-chirality pairs on a 2D grid with contour winding integrals, an optional direction-dependent step speed A(theta) with single-domain or {110} cyclic-twin averaging, a closed-terrace-ring Fourier polygonization measurement, a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn perforation model whose per-sheet footprint is slaved to the terrace tier and whose bridge site is the early-phi argmax, a sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep, a 12-species BCF pitch/omega regression, a DoG lamellar-seam segmentation of one SEM micrograph, and 7 Lean 4 theorems on the integer/rational skeleton of these laws; transfer_boundary: The 'eikonal solver' is kinematic: terrace phases are closed-form Cabrera-Levine travel functions divided by A(theta), not a time-stepped front-propagation PDE, and the subcritical vs supercritical dipole regime is selected by an `if` on d <= 2 r_c rather than emerging from the dynamics | The membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets (no through-thickness phi(z)) at dx = 0.1875 um, so a perforation patch stands for a cluster of 40-60 nm bridges; the bridge site is the argmax of early phi, not a resolved growth-through-pore process; S_0, beta, eps, pore amplitude/width/density are model parameters tuned so that both regimes perforate on the grid | The 12-species lambda_obs / omega_obs table is within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and is not traceable to a measured table in the cited papers; r = 0.9999 therefore tests the table's construction, not the biology | The SEM um/px calibration (0.019867 um/px) was anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um because the Wikimedia micrograph has no scale bar; only the dimensionless CV and aspect ratio are calibration-independent | e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic anisotropy amplitude; twin averaging is a mean-field superposition of A(theta) with no explicit twin boundaries in the spiral core; does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D phase-field of the chitin membrane, resolution of individual mineral bridges, a derived (not templated) gastropod tower lattice, a time-dependent eikonal or BCF step-flow simulation, literature-digitised species pitch/omega observations, an independently calibrated SEM scale, or validated values of e_6, S_0, beta or the pore statistics]; other sources: Crystal structures of aragonite, strontianite, and witherite <http://www.minsocam.org/ammin/AM56/AM56_758.pdf>" ;
