<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Code-to-model traceability: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The header docstring (L1-82) maps Laws 1-5 to the source sections and to the named Lean theorems; the Pass 3 functions cite Cartwright & Checa (2007) Sec. 4 and Checa et al. (2011) for bridges (L724-726, L733-735), De Villiers (1971) for the lattice (L117-122, L535-541) and give the equations in their docstrings (L534-541, L567-574). Deductions: e_6 = 0.15 is a free parameter flagged as such but with no source (L123) (-3); the tower template constants pitch_tower/tower_spacing/hex_mod carry no citation (L497-510) (-4); the pore amplitude/width/density and S_0, beta, eps values are 'model parameters' in the Pass 3 JSON without a stated derivation (-3); the solver docstring's 'eikonal' wording overstates a closed-form phase construction (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py L117–L123: Lattice constants cite De Villiers 1971; E6_DEFAULT = 0.15 is declared a free kinetic amplitude with no source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py#L117-L123>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Gibbs-Thomson v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the BCF/Cabrera-Levine spiral kinematics are the source's (`compute_bcf_spiral_kinematics`, L189-222; `gibbs_thomson_step_velocity`, L224-236), and the Pass 3 additions are genuine model components: a driven Allen-Cahn perforation field with the correct double-well derivative and spinodal threshold S_crit = S_0 + 1/(3 beta) (L713, L765-767), a footprint slaved to the eikonal terrace tier (L736), and a direction-dependent step speed with crystallographic e_2 and a three-domain twin average (L545-552) entering every regime's travel function (L319-321, L338-340, L354-356). Deductions: the terrace fields are closed-form Cabrera-Levine phases and the subcritical/supercritical switch is an `if` on d <= 2 r_c (L308), with `activity` only gating the height field (L337, L344) — the docstring's 'eikonal solver' is kinematic, not a propagated front (-5); the gastropod tower lattice in `simulate_nacre_architecture_3d` is a hard-coded template (pitch_tower = 3.6071, tower_spacing = 11.5, hex_mod = 1 + 0.06 cos 6 theta, L497-510), not an output of the eikonal or membrane model (-4); the membrane model is 2D-per-sheet with the bridge site taken as argmax of early phi (L776-777) and tuning choices n_pores >= 1 (L742), eroded-interior seeding (L745) and a fixed A_g ~ 1/sigma^2 bridge budget (L727-728) (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py L496–L512: Gastropod tower lattice is a hard-coded presentation template (pitch_tower, tower_spacing, hex_mod), not driven by the eikonal or membrane model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py#L496-L512>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Morphometric validation: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1666-1835) now returns 15 reference-anchored measurements, and the Pass 3 ones are honest: raw spiral pitch 7.8007 vs 7.9736 um (L1715-1722, blend removed), columnar offset 0.000 vs 0 (L1775-1783), sheet offset 0.215 vs nominal 0.5 with the under-prediction stated (L1785-1793), sweep transition 0.125 vs the model-analytic 0.121 (L1795-1803), f_2/f_6 vs analytic (L1805-1823), twin angle parity (L1825-1833), and the SEM h_0 method string now carries the calibration caveat (L1748). Deductions: measurements 1-3 (L1684-1713) regress against a 12-species table whose lambda_obs/omega_obs are within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and are untraceable to any measured table, so r = 0.9999 is circular (-8); measurements 7-9 depend on a calibration anchored to the reference value, only CV and aspect ratio being calibration-independent (-4); measurements 13-14 reproduce the analytic f_2/f_6 to 4 digits because T^-1 is nearly linear at the measured ring, validating the implementation more than the physics (-3); measurement 12's reference is the model's own analytic threshold (-2); the sheet-mode offset misses the nominal 0.5 by 2.7 SD (-3); no morphometric compares the model to a literature bridge-offset or tablet-polygonality measurement (e.g. Checa et al. 2011) (-3). Offsetting credit for the honest 2 % raw-pitch deficit and field-counted terrace numbers (7/6/13 vs refs 6/6/12)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json L78–L89: 12-species lambda_obs_um / omega_obs_rad_hr within ~1 % of lambda_pred for every species; not traceable to a measured table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json#L78-L89>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-measurement-12-species-bcf-spiral-terrace-pitch-correlation-cartwright-checa-2007-bcf-1951>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-measurement-12-species-spiral-angular-rotation-frequency-correlation-omega-omega-0-v-inf-r-c>,
