<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — MorphoEval overall 85.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) remediated evaluation of `2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py` (85.2/100, down from the v2 consensus 91.4/100 because the remediation exposed unverified v2 credit; see header). Both v2 remediation items are closed as reduced models: a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn chitin-membrane perforation model coupled to the 2D terrace tier (`simulate_membrane_perforation_phase_field_3d`, L647-814) makes the mineral-bridge stacking offset emergent (columnar 0.000 D_tab vs ref 0; sheet 0.215 D_tab vs nominal 0.5; sweep transition at sigma = 0.125 D_tab vs analytic 0.121), and aragonite [100]/[010] step-velocity anisotropy with {110} cyclic twinning (`aragonite_step_velocity_anisotropy`, L526-552) is wired into the spiral solver and measured on closed terrace rings (f_2 = 0.0738, f_6 = 0.9474 vs analytic). The v2 self-referential pitch blend was removed (raw pitch 7.8007 vs 7.9736 um), terrace counts are now measured, `--seed` is live, and 3 more Lean 4 theorems (7 total, 0 sorry) are verified. The remaining defects are structural: the 12-species observation table is circular, the SEM calibration is anchored to the value it reports, the tower lattice in panels A/C is templated, and the terrace solver is kinematic with a prescribed regime switch. Overall 85.2/100 (faithfulness 84.1, reproducibility 87.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_comparison.png: rendered output of 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py at e651a8b8, image/png, 1988335 B, 2620×2219 px, artifact_sha256 783e8dff611789f803e2347b93f2a800d17da83e277f9b6edc9ca0174d15f68b (sha256 783e8dff611789f803e2347b93f2a800d17da83e277f9b6edc9ca0174d15f68b), spec_fingerprint 4c231c8398be9a26483bc4175fe15077a90c9e9b18a12deaf2c2e4265b43d447. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 4c231c8398be9a26483bc4175fe15077a90c9e9b18a12deaf2c2e4265b43d447; artifact_sha256: 783e8dff611789f803e2347b93f2a800d17da83e277f9b6edc9ca0174d15f68b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_aragonite_tablets_specimen.jpg=e4c6590464523f21..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json=580b05d6121d9596..., datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/scout_manifest.json=6084a2ce133990fc...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cartwright & Checa (2007): nacre grows by Burton-Cabrera-Frank screw-dislocation spiral and target terraces on the mineral surface, with a periodic stack of beta-chitin inter-lamellar membranes (h_0 ~ 0.5 um) whose pores admit mineral bridges that nucleate the next tablet (Sec. 4); columnar (gastropod) nacre stacks tablets vertically, sheet (bivalve) nacre staggers them like bricks | Cartwright et al. (2009): spiral and target patterns in bivalve nacre arise from screw dislocations and Frank-Read-type dislocation pairs; opposite-chirality pairs separated by more than 2 r_c emit closed target terraces | Burton, Cabrera & Frank (1951): Gibbs-Thomson curved-step velocity v(r) = v_inf (1 - r_c / r) and the rotating Archimedean spiral with pitch lambda_0 = (2 pi / omega_0) r_c ~ 19 r_c | Checa, Cartwright & Willinger (2011) and Schäffer et al. (1997): mineral bridges (tens of nm) pass through pores of the inter-lamellar membrane and connect vertically stacked tablets | De Villiers (1971): orthorhombic aragonite lattice constants a = 4.9611, b = 7.9672, c = 5.7407 A; reconstructed_in_script: Closed-form Cabrera-Levine phase fields for single screw, supercritical/subcritical Frank-Read dipoles and same-chirality pairs on a 2D grid with contour winding integrals, an optional direction-dependent step speed A(theta) with single-domain or {110} cyclic-twin averaging, a closed-terrace-ring Fourier polygonization measurement, a stacked-sheet driven Allen-Cahn perforation model whose per-sheet footprint is slaved to the terrace tier and whose bridge site is the early-phi argmax, a sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep, a 12-species BCF pitch/omega regression, a DoG lamellar-seam segmentation of one SEM micrograph, and 7 Lean 4 theorems on the integer/rational skeleton of these laws; transfer_boundary: The 'eikonal solver' is kinematic: terrace phases are closed-form Cabrera-Levine travel functions divided by A(theta), not a time-stepped front-propagation PDE, and the subcritical vs supercritical dipole regime is selected by an `if` on d <= 2 r_c rather than emerging from the dynamics | The membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets (no through-thickness phi(z)) at dx = 0.1875 um, so a perforation patch stands for a cluster of 40-60 nm bridges; the bridge site is the argmax of early phi, not a resolved growth-through-pore process; S_0, beta, eps, pore amplitude/width/density are model parameters tuned so that both regimes perforate on the grid | The 12-species lambda_obs / omega_obs table is within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species and is not traceable to a measured table in the cited papers; r = 0.9999 therefore tests the table's construction, not the biology | The SEM um/px calibration (0.019867 um/px) was anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um because the Wikimedia micrograph has no scale bar; only the dimensionless CV and aspect ratio are calibration-independent | e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic anisotropy amplitude; twin averaging is a mean-field superposition of A(theta) with no explicit twin boundaries in the spiral core; does_not_claim: A volumetric 3D phase-field of the chitin membrane, resolution of individual mineral bridges, a derived (not templated) gastropod tower lattice, a time-dependent eikonal or BCF step-flow simulation, literature-digitised species pitch/omega observations, an independently calibrated SEM scale, or validated values of e_6, S_0, beta or the pore statistics." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:1066-1370 — panel A/B/C titles still collide at the 17 x 16.2 in figure size; shorten them as was done for G/H/I, and document the ~60 s render / ~21 s CPU self-test timing and CLI flags in datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/README.md.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:123 and 1805-1823 — e_6 = 0.15 is a free kinetic amplitude and the f_2/f_6 checks reproduce the analytic factors to 4 digits because T^-1 is nearly linear at the measured ring; anchor e_6 to a measured aragonite tablet polygonality (e.g. tablet-outline Fourier amplitude from Checa et al. 2011 SEM) and measure polygonization on the spiral core (first turn, where the log term matters) rather than only on ring n = 2.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:307-315 and 329-346 — the subcritical vs supercritical Frank-Read decision is an `if` on d <= 2 r_c and activity = tanh(...) (L337) gates only height_um (L344), not psi; the terrace fields are closed-form Cabrera-Levine phases. Either time-step the Gibbs-Thomson front (true eikonal / level-set) so annihilation vs target emission emerges from d, or rename the docstrings from 'eikonal solver' to 'kinematic Cabrera-Levine construction'.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:496-512 — `simulate_nacre_architecture_3d` 'gastropod_columnar_towers' hard-codes pitch_tower = 3.6071, tower_spacing = 11.5, 8 layers and hex_mod = 1 + 0.06 cos 6 theta; derive the tower lattice from the membrane model's bridge centroids (L779) and the twin-polygonized contour (L561-601) so panels A/C are outputs of the Pass 3 models rather than a template.",
        "remediation needed: 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:647-814 — the membrane model is a stack of 2D sheets at dx = 0.1875 um with the bridge site = argmax of early phi (L776) and tuning choices n_pores >= 1 (L742), eroded-interior seeding (L745), fixed A_g ~ 1/sigma^2 (L727-728) and stack termination on non-perforation (L774); add a through-thickness phi(z) or at least a resolved bridge-growth-through-pore step, refine dx to resolve single bridges in a sub-domain, and justify or sweep S_0, beta, eps and the pore statistics so the sheet-mode offset (0.215 vs nominal 0.5, measurement 11 at L1785-1793) is tested rather than reported.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json:38-44 with 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:993-1062 and 1744-1773 — calibration_um_per_px = 0.019867 is 0.50 / 25.1677, i.e. chosen so that h_0 = 0.50 um; replace the scale-bar-less Wikimedia micrograph with a scale-barred SEM (e.g. a Checa/Cartwright figure under a reusable licence) or report h_0 only in px and promote the calibration-independent CV and aspect ratio to the primary specimen measurements.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json:78-89 with 2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py:925-988 and 1684-1713 — the 12-species lambda_obs_um / omega_obs_rad_hr columns lie within ~1 % of the BCF law for every species (r = 0.9999) and cite no measured table; replace them with digitised values from Cartwright & Checa (2007) Table/Fig. or Checa et al. (2011) tablet metrics for the species that have them, drop the rest, and retitle measurements 1-3 as a parity check until then.",
        "remediation needed: morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-073.json (slug 'foraminifera-chamber-spiral') and the Pass 3 prompt (Berger 1969, Globigerinoides ruber) do not match the script, dataset, Lean module or any audit of this slot, which all concern molluscan nacre; reconcile the campaign metadata (slug, paper, organism) with the actual simulation before Pass 4 so the run/dispatch provenance chain is consistent." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.52e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The new sigma / D_tab bridge-localisation sweep (8 values x 3 seeds, L864-883) monotonically moves the mean stacking offset from 0 (columnar) to staggered with the transition at 0.10-0.125 D_tab, and the e_6 sweep (L613-621) moves the 6-fold polygonization monotonically with the twin factor retained; both are rendered in panel I (L1467). The 4 chiral regimes and the 12-species table are exercised as before (L887-920, L925-988), and `--v-inf`, `--r-c`, `--h-0`, `--dipole-d`, `--e6` and a now-live `--seed` are wired into the render (L1955-1980). Deductions: the subcritical/supercritical regime is chosen by the `if` at L308 rather than by sweeping d through 2 r_c (-4); r_c is not swept into the tower lattice, whose geometry is templated (L497-510), so the gastropod/bivalve architecture axis of panel A/C is not parameter-controlled (-5); the sheet-mode alignment index 0.417 vs ref 0 shows the 0.15 D_tab threshold is coarse for 4.2 um tablets (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py L307–L315: Subcritical regime selected by `if` on the input d <= 2 r_c, not by a swept dynamical transition <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2007-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces.py#L307-L315>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`self_test()` (L1838-1950) runs 12 checks: SHA-256 provenance of 6 files, JSON parity, Gibbs-Thomson arrest, 4-regime winding numbers, raw pitch within 4 % and terrace counts within +/-1, 3D heights, 12-species collapse, SEM segmentation, bitwise two-run determinism of the 2D solver, twin parity and analytic factors with the anisotropy-off bitwise-identity check (L1911-1914), membrane behaviour with footprint-in-tier and dt-stability assertions (L1917-1932), seeded bitwise determinism of the phase field (L1935-1937), and the 15-measurement reference anchoring (L1940-1942); it passed 12/12 in this loop (~21 s CPU). `--seed` now seeds the pore field (L1962, L1980) and `requirements.lock.txt` pins the environment. Deductions: the default render is ~60 s wall and the PNG is gitignored, so the committed artifact is the GIF only (-3); self-test timing is not stated in the docstring and no MPLCONFIGDIR note (-2); the sheet mode yields only 2-3 sheets per run, so its statistics rest on 5 seeds (-2); the Pass 3 dataset README is 20 lines and does not list the CLI (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Source and data traceability: 85/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Six dataset files are SHA-256 pinned and verified fail-closed at every run (`EXPECTED_SHA256` L126-146; `verify_dataset_integrity` L160-172), including the new `membrane_perforation_twinning_reference.json` and `pass3_citations.bib` (De Villiers 1971, Schäffer 1997 doi 10.1021/cm960429i, Checa 2011 doi 10.1016/j.jsb.2011.09.011); the four v2 DOIs are unchanged and the dataset README documents the Pass 3 additions and caveats (README L12-20). Deductions: the 12-species observation table (JSON L78-89) has no resolvable source for its lambda_obs/omega_obs values and is now labelled illustrative rather than replaced (-6); the SEM specimen has no scale bar and the calibration is self-referential (JSON L38-44) (-3); the three new DOIs/URL were entered offline and could not be verified in this loop (-2); the slot dispatch record and the Pass 3 prompt carry a foraminifera/Berger (1969) identity that does not match the script, dataset or Lean module, so the campaign-level provenance of this slot is inconsistent (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json L78–L89: 12-species table: observation columns not traceable to any cited measured table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json#L78-L89>",
        "morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-073.json L1–L30: slug 'foraminifera-chamber-spiral' vs nacre script/dataset/audits: campaign metadata mismatch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/morphoeval/cloud/dispatches/slot-073.json#L1-L30>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.5e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cartwright & Checa (2007) & Cartwright et al. (2009) nacre screw-dislocation spirals, Frank-Read target terraces, defect pair annihilation, chitin-membrane perforation bridges and aragonite twin polygonization — Morphological realism / specimen match: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The 9-panel figure shows visually distinct morphologies: Archimedean spiral, closed target rings, interlocked double spiral and the annihilated dipole (panels B-D), the SEM specimen with ROI and detected seams (panel E), the stacked membrane sheets with the perforation patch and bridge centroids (panel G), and the twin-polygonized vs single-domain terrace contours overlaid (panel H), which read as the pseudo-hexagonal tablet habit the source describes. The new membrane-perforation GIF animates sheet-1 perforation. Deductions: the SEM um/px calibration was chosen to return h_0 = 0.50 um (JSON L38-39) and the reference spacing/aspect/layers/CV were copied from the script's own segmentation output, so the specimen panel confirms itself rather than being matched to the source's scale (-8); no side-by-side with Cartwright & Checa's own micrographs or Cartwright et al. (2009) figures of spirals/targets is drawn, leaving the match to the viewer (-5); the panel A/C towers are the hard-coded template (L496-512) (-3); long titles still collide in panels A/B/C at 17 in width (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json L38–L44: calibration_um_per_px = 0.019867 = 0.50 / 25.1677 anchored to h_0 = 0.50 um; reference px spacing, aspect ratio, layers and CV copied from the script's own output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces/nacre_spiral_dislocation_terraces_reference.json#L38-L44>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-cartwright-nacre-spiral-dislocation-terraces-specimen-match-2>,
